\ A waiter queued behind a borrowed hold is served when the borrow ends: the
\ restore delegates onward to a queued waiter the restored owner awaits, since
\ that owner's own release can never come first. The marker order pins both
\ the serialization and the onward delegation: CHAIN-B-END before CHAIN-C,
\ CHAIN-C before CHAIN-OUTER-END.

use "testing" ;

"a queued waiter is served across a restore" test-section

use "./task_load_delegate_chain_outer.1z" ;

chain-outer-word "chain-outer" "the outer module completed its load" assert=

use "./task_load_delegate_chain_b.1z" ;

chain-b-word "chain-b" "the borrowing child's module loaded" assert=

use "./task_load_delegate_chain_c.1z" ;

chain-c-word "chain-c" "the queued child's module loaded after the restore" assert=
